 ## Background
-GaussianBody is introduced for dynamic digital human modeling based on monocular video [S1][S2, unofficial]. The original paper is cited as [216] in [S1] and [214] in [S2, unofficial] [S1][S2, unofficial]. It builds on 3DGS by incorporating physically-based priors to regularize Gaussians in canonical space [S1][S2, unofficial]. It is part of the family of application-specific reconstructions that modify the 3DGS optimization loop with domain-specific constraints [Application-Specific Reconstructions](9269-application-specific-reconstructions.md).
+GaussianBody was introduced in the context of dynamic digital human modeling based on monocular video [S1][S2, unofficial]. It builds on the principles of 3D Gaussian Splatting but extends them with physically-based priors to handle the complexities of dynamic cloth [S1][S2, unofficial]. The method is cited as reference [214] in the source literature [S1][S2, unofficial].
 
